                            <comment id="498293" author="adilger" created="Tue, 21 Jul 2026 19:27:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This is hanging the testing consistently with 2.16 clients (with 2.16 and master servers), even though the 2.16.0 clients &lt;b&gt;should&lt;/b&gt; have the correct UDIO alignment support from patches &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/53997&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/53997&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17525&quot; title=&quot;Unaligned DIO interop with different page sizes fails&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-17525&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17525&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; llite: unaligned DIO interop page alignment&quot;), &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/56775&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/56775&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17525&quot; title=&quot;Unaligned DIO interop with different page sizes fails&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-17525&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17525&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; llite: soft fail unaligned dio&quot;) and &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/56571&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/56571&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18284&quot; title=&quot;interop sanity test_119e test_119f: UDIO files differ, bsize 1048575, 2.12 servers crash&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18284&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18284&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; llite: disallow udio exceptions&quot;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Just skipping the test is not sufficient, even though it would stop the interop test failures, because this will still cause real issues with 2.16+ clients (and any that backported UDIO) hanging when they interact with 2.18+ servers.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
